        dict(kind='wide', title='Check a single answer in five steps before it leaves your desk',
             visual=dict(kind='l09_routine'),
             caption='Each step catches a failure from today. Take more steps when an error costs more.',
             notes='A test set checks a tool; a single answer needs a routine. One, source: ask for the page or clause, and open it. That catches invented facts and missed pages. Two, recount: redo every number by hand or in a spreadsheet, which catches wrong totals. Three, compare: check the key or a second source, which catches sources that disagree. Four, run twice: ask again, and treat a different answer as a warning, because, as Session 5 showed, each run can come out differently. Five, sign: a named person decides and records it. You will not take all five every time. The more an error would cost, the more steps you take.'),
